With a common cathode RGB LED, the configuration for setting the colors is slightly different than with a common anode LED. In a common cathode RGB LED, the cathodes of the LED colors are connected together to ground, and you need to send a HIGH signal (typically 0V in the case of a cathode configuration) to turn on a color.

### Adjusted Code for Common Cathode RGB LED

